//
// The data elements that present a collection: a list, a feed, a timeline, a
// gallery, a board and a calendar. Each takes its items and builds every
// item's content with the view's own item template (`item` bound to it); an
// accessor (`at: e => e.occurredAt`) arrives as the closure it transpiles to.
//
// An item is activatable from the keyboard as well as the pointer when the
// element declares `onClick`. A list, a feed and a calendar show the derived
// empty-state text when there is nothing to show. Over a paginated binding a
// list, a timeline, a gallery, a board and a calendar offer next/previous; a
// feed keeps every page it loaded and loads the next one as its end scrolls
// into view (or from its "load more" action).
//
// A board shows one column per member of its column enum, in declaration
// order. A card moves by drag and drop, or from the keyboard: ArrowLeft and
// ArrowRight move the focused card to the neighbouring column. Either way the
// board reports the move; the app's `onMove` decides what a move does (the
// board never reorders its own data).
//
// A calendar shows a month, a week or a day -- the user's own toggle -- with
// weeks starting on Monday (ISO 8601); a date-only value is a calendar day in
// the user's own time zone. Its days are a keyboard grid with one tab stop:
// the arrow keys move a day or a week, Home and End go to the week's first
// and last day, Page Up and Page Down turn the period, and moving past the
// shown period turns to the period that holds the new day.

